{"name":"Cider Spice","hex":"#ae8167","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cider","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic, often sparkling (carbonated) beverage made from fermented apples.","This or any similar alcoholic drink made from similar fruit, such as pears."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cider"},{"term":"spice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aromatic or pungent plant matter (usually dried) used to season or flavor food.","The quality of being spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add spice or spices to; season.","To spice up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cider","blocks":[{"text":"Cider is an alcoholic beverage made from the fermented juice of apples. The juice of most varieties of apple can be used to make cider, but cider apples are most desirable. The addition of sugar or extra fruit before a second fermentation increases the ethanol content of the resulting beverage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Midwest_hard_cider.jpg/330px-Midwest_hard_cider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cider"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg/500px-Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg/1280px-Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg/500px-Somerset_Cider_Jugs_%282518375463%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cider jugs in Somerset, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASomerset_Cider_Jugs_(2518375463).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg/500px-Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg/1280px-Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg/500px-Tou_d%27preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Few traditional horse-drawn circular cider presses are still in use. Many may still be seen used as garden ornaments, flower planters, or architectural features.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATou_d'preinseu%2C_Morel_Farm%2C_J%C3%A8rri.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Cider_making_Jers